        <html:li>What is formalised and to what depth — <fr:link href="/dhsorens-002Q/" title="The Sumcheck Protocol" uri="https://derekhsorensen.com/dhsorens-002Q/" display-uri="dhsorens-002Q" type="local">sumcheck</fr:link>, <fr:link href="/dhsorens-003G/" title="Spartan and Sumcheck-Based SNARKs" uri="https://derekhsorensen.com/dhsorens-003G/" display-uri="dhsorens-003G" type="local">Spartan</fr:link>, <fr:link href="/dhsorens-0037/" title="FRI" uri="https://derekhsorensen.com/dhsorens-0037/" display-uri="dhsorens-0037" type="local">FRI</fr:link>, <fr:link href="/dhsorens-003B/" title="STIR" uri="https://derekhsorensen.com/dhsorens-003B/" display-uri="dhsorens-003B" type="local">STIR</fr:link>, <fr:link href="/dhsorens-003C/" title="WHIR" uri="https://derekhsorensen.com/dhsorens-003C/" display-uri="dhsorens-003C" type="local">WHIR</fr:link>, <fr:link href="/dhsorens-003J/" title="Binius" uri="https://derekhsorensen.com/dhsorens-003J/" display-uri="dhsorens-003J" type="local">Binius</fr:link>, Merkle trees, coding theory.</html:li>
        <html:li><html:code>ProofSystem/ConstraintSystem</html:code>: R1CS, Plonk, lookup, and memory checking in one place.</html:li>
        <html:li>The security definitions in <html:code>OracleReduction/Security</html:code>, which are the real contribution.</html:li>
        <html:li>What is a statement with no proof yet, and what the roadmap prioritises.</html:li>
        <html:li>Which developments are blocked on <fr:link href="/dhsorens-0041/" title="CompPoly" uri="https://derekhsorensen.com/dhsorens-0041/" display-uri="dhsorens-0041" type="local">CompPoly</fr:link>.</html:li></html:ul></html:p>
